Dear Scott,

Unlike cDNA arrays Affymetrix arrays use between 11 and 20 
oligonucleotides per transcript. These oligos were placed in one line on 
the first Hu6800 array, but since a long time these oligos are scattered 
randomly across the whole array, in order to prevent spatial effects.

The images of your arrays are all ok.
You can see some weird examples at:
http://plmimagegallery.bmbolstad.com/

Best regards
Christian
